course: dictionary
lesson: 5343
title: Kid: child, goat, or joke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word kid has three meanings, so context tells you which one is meant. Most often a kid is a child or a young person. «Ollie's brother saw it and made the older kid give the cards back.» Someone older made a young person give the cards back, so kid means a child here.
explain: Ask what fits the words around it. If the sentence is about a farm, a baby animal, or a field, kid may mean a young goat. If the sentence is about a joke or a tease, kid is a verb meaning to joke.
explain: «Just kidding» means «I was joking». Kidding is a verb here, a friendly way of teasing. If you can swap in «joking» and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Kid means a child or a young person, as in «Ollie's brother saw it and made the older kid give the cards back.»
fact: A kid is also a young goat.
fact: To kid means to joke or tease in a friendly way: «just kidding» means «I was joking».
fact: Kid is an everyday, friendly word, while child is more formal.
fact: At festive dinners even kids raise their juice and shout «gānbēi!» (cheers!), a sign of respect.
exercise: «Ollie's brother saw it and made the older kid give the cards back.» What does kid mean here? | *A child | A young goat | A joke | A kids' menu
exercise: Mia says, «Are you kidding?» What does she mean? | Are you lost? | Are you feeding a goat? | Are you a child? | *Are you joking?
exercise: Which word is more formal than kid? | Kidding | *Child | Kids' menu | Kids
test: «The kid stood by the fence and watched the goats.» What does kid mean here? | *A young goat | A kids' menu | A joke | A child
test: Dad said, «Just kidding!» and laughed. What does kidding mean? | Teasing with anger | Running away fast | *Joking | Giving money to someone
exam: In «The kid fed the baby goat next to the fence», what does kid mean? | *A child | A joke | A young goat | A kids' menu
